{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "8fe1931f-1864-8bb9-8be7-f38d8769f01e",
  "created_at": "2026-01-11T12:11:58-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Rosemarie Santoro",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:08:11-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works storm line, this is Denise."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:08:15-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello, yes. Um, I know it is Sunday, City Hall is closed, I think. But I see this number is for the storm, so I call it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:08:26-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You've got the right place. The storm line is open this weekend. What's going on?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:08:33-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I have water in my cellar. From the storm, the one Friday and Saturday, yesterday it finished. Few inches, maybe, on the floor. In all my years in this house, never. Never one time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:08:47-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, that's no good. What's the address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:08:51-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "One ninety-six Rhode Island Avenue. On the Hill."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:08:55-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "One ninety-six Rhode Island Avenue. And where do you think the water's coming from?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:09:01-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I think, the street. The water, it comes down and the, the drain, in front, it does not take it. And now the sidewalk is, how you say, a sheet of mud. Mud and, um, grit. Sand, little stones. All over. You cannot walk without you slip."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:09:19-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So the drain out front is clogged with debris, it sounds like, and it washed all that onto the sidewalk."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:09:27-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, yes. Full of, of the stuff. And every time I think, somebody will come and clean. Nobody comes. Now it is in my house."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:09:37-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I hear you. Let me get this down. Is the water still coming in, or is it just sitting down there now?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:09:46-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Just sitting. It is not more coming. Yesterday night it stopped."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:09:51-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, good. Any electrical down there, a furnace, a panel, that's sitting in it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:09:57-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The furnace is, is up a little on the blocks. I think it is okay. I am not touching."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:10:05-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Smart. Leave it alone for now. I'm going to put in a request for crews to look at the catch basin at that address and the debris on the sidewalk."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:10:17-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A work order? You open a work order? And, um, what date? What day they come? This is what I need to know."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:10:26-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, I'm opening it now. After a storm like this the crews are working through a long list, so I'd say the next few days, probably early to middle of the week. I'll mark it as water getting into a home, which moves it up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:10:44-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Early week. Okay. Monday, Tuesday?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:10:47-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Monday or Tuesday is what I'd hope for, but I'm putting it in as priority. Can I get a callback number in case dispatch needs to reach you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:10:58-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. Four zero one, five five five, zero one six four."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:11:03-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, zero-one-six-four. Got it. Is that your landline?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:11:07-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, the house phone. Oh, excuse me, it is ringing now. [pause] It is my mother. She calls two times every day, morning and, um, afternoon. I let it ring. I cannot talk about this and also her."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:11:22-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Go ahead and let it ring, we're nearly done. Your name for the request?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:11:28-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Rosemarie Santoro. S, A, N, T, O, R, O."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:11:32-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, Ms. Santoro. You're all set, the request is in for the drain at one ninety-six Rhode Island Avenue and the sidewalk. If more water comes in before then, call this line back."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:11:46-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Thank you. I hope they come. Really, I hope."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:11:51-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'll flag it. Take care, and watch your step out there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T12:11:56-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. Goodbye."
    }
  ],
